#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:1
msgid "Autolinker.js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:3
msgid ""
"Because I had so much trouble finding a good auto-linking implementation "
"out in the wild, I decided to roll my own. It  seemed that everything I "
"found out there was either an implementation that didn't cover every "
"case, or was just limited in one way or another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:8
msgid "So, this utility attempts to handle everything. It:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:10
msgid ""
"Autolinks URLs, whether or not they start with the protocol (i.e. "
"'http://'). In other words, it will automatically link the text "
"\"google.com\", as well as \"http://google.com\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:13
msgid "Will properly handle URLs with special characters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:14
msgid ""
"Will properly handle URLs with query parameters or a named anchor (i.e. "
"hash)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:15
msgid "Will autolink email addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:16
msgid "Will autolink phone numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:17
msgid "Will autolink Twitter handles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:18
msgid "Will autolink hashtags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:19
msgid ""
"Will properly handle HTML input. The utility will not change the `href` "
"attribute inside anchor (&lt;a&gt;) tags (or any other tag/attribute for "
"that matter), and will not accidentally wrap the inner text of an anchor "
"tag with a new one (which would cause doubly-nested anchor tags)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:24
msgid "Hope that this utility helps you as well!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:26
msgid ""
