#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:96
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:98
msgid ""
"These are the options which may be specified for linking. These are "
"specified by providing an Object as the second parameter to "
"[Autolinker.link()](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-static-method-link). These include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:101
msgid ""
"[newWindow](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-newWindow) : Boolean<br /> `true` to have the links "
"should open in a new window when clicked, `false` otherwise. Defaults to "
"`true`.<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:104
msgid ""
"[stripPrefix](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-stripPrefix) : Boolean<br /> `true` to have the 'http://'"
" or 'https://' and/or the 'www.' stripped from the beginning of links, "
"`false` otherwise. Defaults to `true`.<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:107
msgid ""
"[truncate](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-truncate) : Number/Object<br /> A number for how many "
"characters long URLs/emails/Twitter handles/Twitter hashtags should be "
"truncated to inside the text of a link. If the match is over the number "
"of characters, it will be truncated to this length by replacing the end "
"of the string with a two period ellipsis ('..').<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:113
msgid ""
"Example: a url like 'http://www.yahoo.com/some/long/path/to/a/file' "
"truncated to 25 characters may look like this: "
"'yahoo.com/some/long/pat..'<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:116
msgid ""
"In the object form, both `length` and `location` may be specified to "
"perform  truncation. Available options for `location` are: 'end' "
"(default), 'middle',  or 'smart'. Example usage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:124
msgid ""
"The 'smart' truncation option is for URLs where the algorithm attempts to"
"  strip out unnecessary parts of the URL (such as the 'www.', then URL "
"scheme,  hash, etc.) before trying to find a good point to insert the "
"ellipsis if it is  still too long. For details, see source code of:  "
"[TruncateSmart](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api/Autolinker.truncate.TruncateSmart)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:129
msgid ""
"[className](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-className) : String<br /> A CSS class name to add to the "
"generated anchor tags. This class will be added to all links, as well as "
"this class plus \"url\"/\"email\"/\"phone\"/\"twitter\"/\"hashtag\" "
"suffixes for styling url/email/phone/twitter/hashtag links differently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:134
msgid "For example, if this config is provided as \"myLink\", then:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:136
msgid "URL links will have the CSS classes: \"myLink myLink-url\"<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:137
msgid "Email links will have the CSS classes: \"myLink myLink-email\"<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:138
msgid "Phone links will have the CSS classes: \"myLink myLink-phone\"<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:139
msgid "Twitter links will have the CSS classes: \"myLink myLink-twitter\"<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:140
msgid "Hashtag links will have the CSS classes: \"myLink myLink-hashtag\"<br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:142
msgid ""
"[urls](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api/Autolinker-"
"cfg-urls) : Boolean/Object<br /> `true` to have URLs auto-linked, `false`"
" to skip auto-linking of URLs. Defaults to `true`.<br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:146
msgid ""
"This option also accepts an Object form with 3 properties, to allow for "
"more customization of what exactly gets linked. All default to `true`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:149
msgid ""
"schemeMatches (Boolean): `true` to match URLs found prefixed with a "
"scheme, i.e. `http://google.com`, or `other+scheme://google.com`, `false`"
" to prevent these types of matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:152
msgid ""
"wwwMatches (Boolean): `true` to match urls found prefixed with `'www.'`, "
"i.e. `www.google.com`. `false` to prevent these types of matches. Note  "
"that if the URL had a prefixed scheme, and `schemeMatches` is true, it  "
"will still be linked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:156
msgid ""
"tldMatches: `true` to match URLs with known top level domains (.com, "
".net, etc.) that are not prefixed with a scheme or `'www.'`. Ex: "
"`google.com`,  `asdf.org/?page=1`, etc. `false` to prevent these types of"
" matches. <br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:161
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Example usage: `urls: { schemeMatches: true, wwwMatches: true, "
"tldMatches: false }`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:163
msgid ""
"[email](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api/Autolinker-"
"cfg-email) : Boolean<br /> `true` to have email addresses auto-linked, "
"`false` to skip auto-linking of email addresses. Defaults to `true`.<br "
"/><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:166
msgid ""
"[phone](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api/Autolinker-"
"cfg-phone) : Boolean<br /> `true` to have phone numbers auto-linked, "
"`false` to skip auto-linking of phone numbers. Defaults to `true`.<br "
"/><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:169
msgid ""
"[twitter](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-twitter) : Boolean<br /> `true` to have Twitter handles "
"auto-linked, `false` to skip auto-linking of Twitter handles. Defaults to"
" `true`.<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:172
msgid ""
"[hashtag](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-hashtag) : Boolean/String<br /> A string for the service "
"name to have hashtags auto-linked to. Supported values at this time are "
"'twitter', 'facebook' and 'instagram'. Pass `false` to skip auto-linking "
"of hashtags. Defaults to `false`.<br /><br />"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/autolinker_README.md:176
msgid ""
"[replaceFn](http://gregjacobs.github.io/Autolinker.js/docs/#!/api"
"/Autolinker-cfg-replaceFn) : Function<br /> A function to use to "
"programmatically make replacements of matches in the input string, one at"
" a time. See the section <a href=\"#custom-replacement-function\">Custom "
"Replacement Function</a> for more details."
msgstr ""

